{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558751965,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf771b7ffeH0MBS4KaNsCAC0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4097063001L7P9a6ZSwHkvr3","sessionID":"ses_e2bf771b7ffeH0MBS4KaNsCAC0","messageID":"msg_1d4095f06001LvtVfNCXLBJe1Y","type":"tool","id":"call_18bb8f9adf9141ada10daaa0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":30,"offset":130,"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md, lines 130-159\n130: **Daemon and freshness.** A chokidar watcher under `lib/daemon/` observes `.skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md`, per-skill `ROUTER.md` and per-skill `graph-metadata.json` files. On change, it triggers an incremental rebuild and refreshes the trust-state vocabulary: `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`.\n131: \n132: **Skill graph.** A SQLite database holds the cross-skill edges (depends_on, dependents, enhances, conflicts) plus per-skill metadata. The `skill_graph_query` command exposes read-only graph traversal.\n133: \n134: **Doc-trigger harvest (flag-gated).** With `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`, the scan harvests reference/asset doc frontmatter into a `skill_docs` table, the watcher tracks those docs for freshness, and the derived lane scores their trigger phrases (top-3 per skill, tier-weighted, 0.45 contribution cap), surfacing sanitized `matchedDocs` paths on recommendations. Default-off with byte-identical flag-off behavior; the Python shim harvests the same phrases under the same flag, and the launcher's `CHILD_ENV_ALLOWLIST` must carry the flag for it to reach the daemon child.\n135: \n136: **Local scorer.** `runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` is called in production. The CLI runs it when the daemon is unreachable, marks the response `degraded` and reports `source: local-scorer`, so a caller gets a stale route rather than no route. The same script keeps the JSON-array facade working for direct callers.\n137: \n138: ---\n139: \n140: ## 5. HOOK AND PLUGIN INTEGRATION\n141: \n142: The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The native adapters and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`; the OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. When the handler has no brief, including after a timeout or a no-route result, it emits the directives fallback and lets the prompt proceed. The Claude adapter applies `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` to its advisor subprocess. When the operator leaves it unset, the Claude shim sets 2,200 ms for the hook under its own 2,500 ms kill so the fallback prints in time. Pi runs the handler in-process and races it against the budget plus 300 ms. The hook's request sends `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. The hook keeps that `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. The OpenCode plugin does not send the option and gets the default of true. The plugin appends the brief to the system prompt and exposes the advisor status tool.\n143: \n144: ---\n145: \n146: ## 6. ENFORCEMENT AND VERIFICATION\n147: \n148: Validation runs at two layers.\n149: \n150: **Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). The code writes them only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n151: \n152: **Test surfaces.** Default `npm test` runs unit and integration suites under `runtime/tests/`. Scorer benchmarks live under `runtime/bench/`. Operator playbook scenarios live in `manual-testing-playbook/`.\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: ## 7. DECISION RECORDS\n157: \n158: | ADR | Subject | Status |\n159: |---|---|---|\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 160]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md, lines 130-159\n130: **Daemon and freshness.** A chokidar watcher under `lib/daemon/` observes `.skilled/skills/*/SKILL.md`, per-skill `ROUTER.md` and per-skill `graph-metadata.json` files. On change, it triggers an incremental rebuild and refreshes the trust-state vocabulary: `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`.\n131: \n132: **Skill graph.** A SQLite database holds the cross-skill edges (depends_on, dependents, enhances, conflicts) plus per-skill metadata. The `skill_graph_query` command exposes read-only graph traversal.\n133: \n134: **Doc-trigger harvest (flag-gated).** With `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS=true`, the scan harvests reference/asset doc frontmatter into a `skill_docs` table, the watcher tracks those docs for freshness, and the derived lane scores their trigger phrases (top-3 per skill, tier-weighted, 0.45 contribution cap), surfacing sanitized `matchedDocs` paths on recommendations. Default-off with byte-identical flag-off behavior; the Python shim harvests the same phrases under the same flag, and the launcher's `CHILD_ENV_ALLOWLIST` must carry the flag for it to reach the daemon child.\n135: \n136: **Local scorer.** `runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` is called in production. The CLI runs it when the daemon is unreachable, marks the response `degraded` and reports `source: local-scorer`, so a caller gets a stale route rather than no route. The same script keeps the JSON-array facade working for direct callers.\n137: \n138: ---\n139: \n140: ## 5. HOOK AND PLUGIN INTEGRATION\n141: \n142: The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The native adapters and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`; the OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. When the handler has no brief, including after a timeout or a no-route result, it emits the directives fallback and lets the prompt proceed. The Claude adapter applies `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` to its advisor subprocess. When the operator leaves it unset, the Claude shim sets 2,200 ms for the hook under its own 2,500 ms kill so the fallback prints in time. Pi runs the handler in-process and races it against the budget plus 300 ms. The hook's request sends `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. The hook keeps that `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. The OpenCode plugin does not send the option and gets the default of true. The plugin appends the brief to the system prompt and exposes the advisor status tool.\n143: \n144: ---\n145: \n146: ## 6. ENFORCEMENT AND VERIFICATION\n147: \n148: Validation runs at two layers.\n149: \n150: **Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). The code writes them only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n151: \n152: **Test surfaces.** Default `npm test` runs unit and integration suites under `runtime/tests/`. Scorer benchmarks live under `runtime/bench/`. Operator playbook scenarios live in `manual-testing-playbook/`.\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: ## 7. DECISION RECORDS\n157: \n158: | ADR | Subject | Status |\n159: |---|---|---|\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 160]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":30,\"offset\":130,\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558750819,"end":1794558751965}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558751975,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf771b7ffeH0MBS4KaNsCAC0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40972c60014CavzGzHNHVcov","sessionID":"ses_e2bf771b7ffeH0MBS4KaNsCAC0","messageID":"msg_1d4095f06001LvtVfNCXLBJe1Y","type":"tool","id":"call_d0c7fd0aef77475c96959a00","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -la .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/ 2>&1","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/:\ntotal 88\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 13 06:59 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 19 michelkerkmeester  staff    608 Nov 13 06:58 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 12 10:24 claude\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 12 10:24 dsh\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 13 06:59 lib\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 12 21:10 pi\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  14665 Nov 12 10:24 skill-advisor-hook-validation.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  25586 Nov 13 06:59 skill-advisor-hook.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 12 10:24 tests\n\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 michelkerkmeester  staff   128 Nov 12 10:24 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff   288 Nov 13 06:59 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  8267 Nov 12 10:24 prompt-advisor.mjs\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  2470 Nov 12 10:24 README.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/:\ntotal 88\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 13 06:59 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 19 michelkerkmeester  staff    608 Nov 13 06:58 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 12 10:24 claude\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 12 10:24 dsh\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 michelkerkmeester  staff    288 Nov 13 06:59 lib\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 12 21:10 pi\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  14665 Nov 12 10:24 skill-advisor-hook-validation.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  25586 Nov 13 06:59 skill-advisor-hook.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 12 10:24 tests\n\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 michelkerkmeester  staff   128 Nov 12 10:24 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 9 michelkerkmeester  staff   288 Nov 13 06:59 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  8267 Nov 12 10:24 prompt-advisor.mjs\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  2470 Nov 12 10:24 README.md\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls -la .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/ 2>&1\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558751430,"end":1794558751975}}}}
