{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558806690,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf771b7ffeH0MBS4KaNsCAC0","part":{"id":"prt_1d40a404f002Sb5GQcy8HmT1ns","sessionID":"ses_e2bf771b7ffeH0MBS4KaNsCAC0","messageID":"msg_1d40a2e14001g4MYvnAdP6pBJd","type":"text","text":"T051 is done. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` now names DSH in the adapter list and describes the DSH adapter in section 5.\n\nFiles written: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` (one line of the section 5 paragraph).\n\nThe change reads: \"The advisor ships prompt-submit adapters for Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, DSH and Pi, plus the OpenCode plugin at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`. The DSH adapter at `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` runs the Claude handler from `runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\"\n\nVerify output, run from the repository root:\n\n```\ncommand1: rg -c \"hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs\" $ARCH\n1\nexit=0\ncommand2: rg -c \"Devin, DSH and Pi\" $ARCH\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nBoth expected counts print 1. The scoped diff shows one changed line and no other file.\n\nI checked the claim against the code before writing it: `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` lines 17-20 resolve `ADVISOR_MODULE_URL` to `../../runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, and its `runAdvisor` calls `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit`. So the sentence matches the adapter.\n\nThe `T051` checkbox is unticked as instructed. Nothing failed and nothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794558804047,"end":1794558806690}}}
